WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:06.680
OK, let's go next to our caller from the six
one four area code, who is finding themselves

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:09.200
on the line today from six one four.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:10.770
Hi, David.

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:16.500
This is Roshini from Powell, Ohio, who lost
Cheaney, OK.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.910
I realizing when you send Super Chat's I've
been mispronouncing your name, but I appreciate

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:21.910
that now.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:23.080
It's OK.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:26.949
Yeah, it's cool that you remember that.

00:00:26.949 --> 00:00:33.699
But I just have a I have a question for like
the longer that the long runs of the progressive

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:39.290
parties, I recently saw a clip from the car
Kolinsky show where he talks about how, you

00:00:39.290 --> 00:00:46.760
know, he gave his input that if the if the
left and progressives want to enact progressive

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:52.799
policies, they would have to take over the
Democratic Party because we're obviously a

00:00:52.799 --> 00:00:53.799
two party system.

00:00:53.799 --> 00:00:56.820
And I was just wondering what your what your
view is on that.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:02.159
Like, do you think that an overrunning of
the other Democratic Party is the way to go

00:01:02.159 --> 00:01:06.659
or do you think a third party is an option
so that, you know, the lesser of two evils

00:01:06.659 --> 00:01:09.270
argument doesn't really exist anymore?

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:10.920
So I was just wondering what you thought about
that.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:13.600
Listen, you really have to work both angles
at the same time.

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:17.170
Obviously, in an ideal system, we wouldn't
have a two party system where if you're not

00:01:17.170 --> 00:01:21.600
a Democrat or a Republican, at least, that
everything other than a local level, you essentially

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:22.600
have no power.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:26.220
Even the few independents in the Senate caucus
with the Democrats in this case, it's Bernie

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:27.220
and Angus King.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:34.759
So I would be working to try to change campaign
finance and how elections are structured,

00:01:34.759 --> 00:01:38.380
which are really the two big issues that we
need to change if a third party is ever going

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:39.380
to have a shot.

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:43.759
But simultaneously, if you only do that and
you don't infiltrate the Democratic Party

00:01:43.759 --> 00:01:47.189
at all, you could lose five, 10, 20 or 100
years.

00:01:47.189 --> 00:01:50.030
I mean, who knows how long that first process
is going to take?

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:51.079
So you need to be doing both.

00:01:51.079 --> 00:01:53.290
You've got to be able to walk and chew gum
at the same time.

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:54.290
Right.

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:55.290
Yeah, yeah, absolutely.

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:59.899
I mean, I just I always thought that the answer
was somewhere in the middle and you don't

00:01:59.899 --> 00:02:02.960
have to kind of go to one side or the other.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:04.060
So, yeah, I appreciate that.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:05.060
Thank you so much.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:06.060
David, thanks for everything you do.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:07.060
All right.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.060
Thank you for the call.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:08.110
Great to hear from you.

